From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:09:38 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 77/77] Plutonium: agents type through the session's keymap,
 and a temporary one for what it lacks

Plutonium.getKeymap returns the keymap Exo sends apps (XKB text) and the
characters its first layout types, each with its key and the modifiers held
for it (shift, AltGr), so the helper maps text through the user's layout
instead of a US one. dispatchWindowKeyEvents takes AltGr (16) in its
modifiers. Plutonium.setWindowKeymap sends a window's client a keymap in place
of the seat's (Seat::SetAgentKeymap(), to the client's keyboards) until it
comes again without one: the helper adds characters the layout lacks to spare
keys of the user's keymap for type_window, and password auto-type can do the
same.
